<title>USA: Four Media cuts IPO pricing range.</title>
<headline>Four Media cuts IPO pricing range.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Four Media Co has cut the price range for shares in its initial public offering to $10 to $12 each from a prior range of $12 to $14 apiece, according to a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>The company provides technical, creative and broadcast services to owners, producers and distributors of television programming. About 5.7 million shares will be offered in the IPO, which is due sometime next week, according to lead underwriter Furman Selz.</p>
